188 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (J. Craig Venter, a trailblazing geneticist and entrepreneur, revolutionized biotechnology by leading the first draft of the human genome at Celera Genomics in 2000. Using shotgun sequencing, he surpassed the Human Genome Project, making genomic research faster and more affordable, thus accelerating medical discoveries.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
189 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (In 2010, Venter achieved a landmark feat by creating Mycoplasma mycoides JCVI-syn1.0, the first synthetic life form. His team designed a genome digitally, synthesized it, and transplanted it into a cell, demonstrating that life could be engineered. This breakthrough opened new frontiers in synthetic biology, enabling applications like custom microbes.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [8]
>>
