<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (NUCLEOTIDE KNOW-IT-ALL : AI ON GENES)
/E (NUCLEOTIDE KNOW-IT-ALL : AI ON GENES)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
211 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Our bodies function based on instructions in our DNA, organized into genes that code for proteins. Small differences in this DNA, called genetic variants, make us unique and can influence our risk for diseases. Understanding these variants is vital for accurate diagnosis and effective treatment.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
212 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Large Language Models \(LLMs\), a type of AI proficient in understanding language patterns, are now being applied to the "language" of DNA. Trained on vast genomic datasets, LLMs use mechanisms like "self-attention" to identify complex patterns within DNA sequences \(A, T, C, G\) and predict how variations might lead to disease.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
213 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Scientists use LLMs to classify genetic variants through several methods. They combine outputs from multiple models \(e.g., GPN-MSA, AlphaMissense\)for more comprehensive predictions. Analyzing both DNA and the resulting protein data provides a fuller picture of a variant's impact. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
214 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Furthermore, general LLMs can be "fine-tuned" on specific genetic data to become experts in variant classification.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
215 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The real-world impact is significant. In heart rhythm disorders, LLMs have drastically improved the classification of previously uncertain variants. They aid in extracting genomic information from cancer reports and help accelerate the diagnosis of rare diseases by analyzing patient data. LLMs are also uncovering insights into the genetic underpinnings of conditions like Alzheimer's disease.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
216 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Using LLMs offers key benefits: improved accuracy in variant classification, especially for uncertain variants; significantly faster analysis of vast genetic datasets, speeding up diagnosis; better handling of biological complexity; and the potential to advance personalized medicine. LLMs also streamline the laborious process of reviewing scientific literature, saving valuable time for researchers and clinicians.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
